      "content": "That's a good start, but I think they both feel a bit too \"thematic\" and polished. I want to see more of their actual arguments. \n\nCan you expand on the traditionalist's monologue? I want them to talk about why preserving certain institutions—like the local school board or long-standing community traditions—is actually the most logical and compassionate way to ensure the town's survival. Make it sound like they are speaking from a place of deep experience and stability.",
